ZGeo change log
===============

Version 1.22.0 — 2026-11-12
Previous GitHub release: v1.15.0 (2026-11-08)

Overview
--------
This changelog covers all changes between the previous public release
(v1.15.0) and version 1.22.0. The main themes are a configurable checks
system, GeoJSON validation, data-quality checks for attributes and
datasets, a full-width progress bar, and a complete Russian/English
interface.

Changes since v1.15.0
---------------------

1.16.0
- The interface can be switched between Russian and English with the
  "EN" / "RU" button in the top-right corner of the panel.
- The selected language is saved in QGIS settings and restored on the
  next launch.

1.17.0
- Clicking "Check Attributes" opens a separate "Checks" window with a
  list of checks.
- Each check has a checkbox, and an "i" button shows its description on
  hover.
- Refinement of layer characteristics and dataset sizes is available as
  a separate check.

1.18.0
- Automatic refinement after the first scan has been removed.
- The "Check Attributes" button has been renamed to "Checks".
- Dataset size, SHP size, MIF/MID size, CRS and feature count are
  available as separate checks, with size first.

1.19.0
- Added the "Check JSON for GeoJSON format" check.
- `.json` and `.geojson` files are validated by the GeoJSON `type` field.
- Files that are not GeoJSON are excluded from the list, and the file
  count, total size and statistics are recalculated.
- The JSON check runs before the other refinements and appears only when
  JSON/GeoJSON files are found.

1.20.0
- Added a progress bar at the bottom of the window.
- It shows indeterminate progress during scanning and the number of
  processed files during checks.

1.20.1
- The progress bar was moved below the status bar and now spans the full
  width of the window.

1.21.0
- Removed the separate "Refine SHP size" and "Refine MIF/MID size"
  checks because "Refine size" already covers all formats, including SHP
  and MIF/MID.

1.22.0
- Added six data-quality checks:
  - "Shapefile field name check" — field name length (10 characters max
    for DBF), spaces and invalid characters.
  - "Truncated field name duplicates check" — field names that collide
    after truncation to 10 characters.
  - "DBF encoding and .cpg check" — missing or empty `.cpg`, unknown
    encoding, unreadable DBF header.
  - "Dataset completeness check" — required files for SHP
    (`.shp + .dbf + .shx`), MIF/MID (`.mif + .mid`) and TAB
    (`.tab + .dat/.map/.id`), case-insensitive.
  - "CRS check" — missing, unknown, partially missing or mixed
    coordinate reference systems.
  - "Empty layers check" — layers without features and files with zero
    features.
- The "Attribute issues" column has been replaced by a unified "Issues"
  column. It shows "Yes", "No" or "—" and contains the full list of
  findings in the cell tooltip.
- "Problem files: N" and the "Only problem files" filter now cover all
  problem checks, not only attribute names.
- The checks window is scrollable and shows 11 checks.
- The checks run in the background with progress reporting and can be
  cancelled; partial results are kept.

What changed in 1.22.0 compared with 1.21.0
-------------------------------------------
- New checks: Shapefile field names, truncated duplicates, DBF encoding
  and `.cpg`, dataset completeness, CRS quality, empty layers.
- Unified "Issues" column instead of the attribute-only column.
- Problem counter and filter include every problem check.
- Updated Russian and English documentation and translations.
- Added unit tests for all new checks and QGIS smoke tests for real
  GeoJSON, SHP and GPKG datasets.

Available checks in 1.22.0
--------------------------
Refinement:
- Refine size
- Refine CRS
- Refine feature count

Validation and problem checks:
- Check JSON for GeoJSON format
- Attribute field name check (non-Latin characters)
- Shapefile field name check
- Truncated field name duplicates check
- DBF encoding and .cpg check
- Dataset completeness check
- CRS check
- Empty layers check

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.22.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

